  "title": "Transients: attacks moved far from the recorded pitch",
  "heading": "Does the attack still sound like the instrument when you play far from the recorded note?",
  "intro": [
    "Each group is one recording played as a short phrase one and two octaves away from its own note. The two takes differ only in how the first fraction of a second of each note is made, in a random order. The plucked groups are the real test; the bowed groups check that nothing gets worse.",
    "Listen to the start of each note: the pick, the click, the strike. Does it keep its real size and snap, or does it turn into a dull thud (down) or a tiny chirp (up)? Then listen for anything unnatural, such as a doubled or detached attack."
  ],
